 ; Each start-up pays for the frame tables of the code linked in: ld.so relocates every descriptor's return address and
 ; the runtime hashes them all into one table. So the release build has no -g: its debug information, which nothing
 ; reads (no backtraces are printed), gave every bounds check a call site of its own (7,370 in the server, piled up in
 ; the table's hash) and every descriptor 4 more bytes. Bounds checks stay, as before.
 (release
  (ocamlopt_flags ())))
